    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0fb8a2b3-228a-5e43-ae27-18911b0a732a" activityNameId="486a3148-09ad-56a0-8ba9-b6b92869df89" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Facilities for mechanical treatment of WEEE scrap</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Facilities for mechanical treatment of WEEE scrap
The data represent an example of a mechanical treatment line for WEEE – comprising an initial shredder, a magnetic separator and an Eddy-current separator, a second (smaller) shredder, followed again by a magnetic separator and an Eddy-current separator – all this linked by conveyor belts. Total weight data are taken from producer information of such machines and own assumptions. Composition, infrastructure and production efforts are based on own assumptions. The dataset represents a production line with a total weight of 35’000 kg. Update 2023: The bill of materials is assumed to remain the same, but the background datasets are updating using new ICT datasets.; Geography: This module relates to the global situation.; UUID: 4442b11b-d3bb-3168-8f20-178bb3b67c58
This module includes material, production efforts (transportation, energy, …) and the infrastructure for the production of all the machineries used for the mechanical treatment of WEEE devices. No information about emissions (air, water) and waste are included.
Location: This module relates to the global situation.
Technology: Typical data of current machines sold for the mechanical treatment of WEEE devices.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4442b11b-d3bb-3168-8f20-178bb3b67c58.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
